From 08d52e1d936a1d19b7d7e47996b4c7711980ef67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:40:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] The guest checks the driver's glibc requirement itself,
 where the runtime is known

The packaging side can measure what Mesa's lavapipe needs and say so, but it cannot know which rootfs
the phone will have: that image is the user's, not an artifact of this repo (uruntime, the one runtime
pinned here, is a bundle of preloads under usr/local/lib - not the guest's /usr/lib). So the decision
moves to the only place both numbers are present. SessionService passes BL_DRIVER_MIN_GLIBC next to
BL_VK_DRIVER - the guest receives the manifest's path, not the driver's directory, so meta.json's
minGlibc could not be read from inside - and droiddeck-session compares it against
`getconf GNU_LIBC_VERSION` before it exports anything.

Three outcomes, deliberately different. Too old: DD_SOFTWARE_GLIBC_OLD and exit 78, because a driver the
loader will refuse produces an empty device list and a Vulkan init error thirty seconds later, which is
not a diagnosis. Unknown (musl, or no getconf): one line in the session log and continue, because
refusing a runtime that is fine on a missing tool would be the app inventing a problem. Undeclared (any
zip built before this): noted, not punished. The "== vulkan driver" line is said on every accepted path,
with the verdict inside it, since that line is what the app shows while it waits.

tools/test/run_software_session_tests.sh executes this branch for real: the block is cut out of the
script by markers - and the test fails loudly if the markers move, instead of quietly testing nothing -
and run in bash against fixtures, with a fake getconf on PATH and driver directories in the shape the
importer leaves them. Eleven cases, including the one that matters most here: a driver whose library is
unreadable is refused, and the probe asserts the loader was pointed at nothing at all. No fallback.

Writing that test found a defect I had introduced an hour earlier in the same block: the "== vulkan
driver" announcement had drifted into the else-branch of the version check, so a rootfs that reported no
glibc would have started with nothing in the log about which driver it drew with. Fixed by making the
verdict a variable and the line unconditional.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
